theorem-4.2"],"id":"euler.theorem-4.2","kind":"claim","label":"Theorem 4.2","locator":"Theorem 4.2, Section 4","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Theorem 4.2.** Assume $H^\\#\\le\\operatorname{Id}$ on $I\\times\\mathbb T^3$ as quadratic forms. For every $L\\in C(I;C^{0,1/2})$ the system (4.9) has a unique solution with $z\\in C^1(I;C^{0,1/2})$, $c\\in C^{0,1/2}$ divergence free and $\\nabla_a\\phi\\in C(I;C^{0,1/2})$. There are absolute $C,p$ such that, with $$\\begin{equation}\n A=C\\bigl(D_-+\\|M\\|_\\infty+\\left\\lVert K\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{1,1/2}}\n   +\\left\\lVert\\Omega\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{1,1/2}}\\bigr)^p, \\tag{4.10}\n\\end{equation}$$ one has $\\left\\lVert v\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{0,1/2}}\\le A\\left\\lVert L\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{0,1/2}}$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.theorem-4.2","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.9","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.9%22%2C%22euler.theorem-4.2%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.9%22%2C%22euler.theorem-4.2%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.theorem-4.2"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.proposition-5.2","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.proposition-5.2%22%2C%22euler.theorem-4.2%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.proposition-5.2%22%2C%22euler.theorem-4